[TdAudioVideoSettingsPC]
ResolutionText=RESOLUTION
ResolutionDesc=Change the resolution that the game will be displayed in. Selecting a higher resolution will improve the look of the game but may impact performance.
VerticalSyncText=VERTICAL SYNC
VerticalSyncDesc=Lock the frame rate from the graphics card to the refresh rate of the monitor. This can resolve issues with texture tearing but may impact performance.
TextureDetailText=TEXTURE DETAIL
TextureDetailDesc=Select the level of texture detail. This will improve the look of the game, by using larger textures, but may impact performance.
GFXQualityText=GRAPHICS QUALITY
GFXQualityDesc=Increase the amount of post-processing effects. This will improve the look of the game but may impact performance.
AudioDeviceText=AUDIO DEVICE
AudioDeviceDesc=Select the audio device to use. If you have either an on-board sound card or a dedicated sound card use 'Hardware' sound to improve performance.
AntiAliasingText=ANTI-ALIASING
AntiAliasingDesc=Toggles anti-aliasing, which produces smoother edges but may impact performance.
PhysXText=PHYSX SUPPORT
PhysXDesc=Physics Hardware Acceleration Settings. The game needs to be restarted when changing this setting.

